    "q-140078": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140078",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Given the transformation\n $T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x+y \\\\ 4z-2x \\\\ z-4x-3y\\end{aligned}],$ find its rank.",
      "worked_solution": "First, the standard matrix of $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Im}(T))=\\text{rank}(T).$ \n\nSo, we need to find the rank of the matrix $T.$ We reduce $T$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $T$ has $3$ pivot columns, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=3.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
